From 2edafbd544998718308466968c64682e3d8c6a25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neo <65333514+neow021@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:59:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(feishu): send anchorless topic messages as in-thread
 replies

Feishu's message.create rejects receive_id_type=thread_id with 99992402, so
every topic send without an inbound message to reply to was dropped: cron
deliver=origin reports, background-process completions and MEDIA files.

_send_raw_message now replies into the topic (reply_in_thread on a message
of that topic, via _reply_into_topic) instead of the invalid create path.
cron's live lane reads thread_fallback/requested_thread_id with
_result_field, so a SendResult no longer raises AttributeError and resends
the report through the standalone path as a duplicate. The old routing test
that asserted receive_id_type=thread_id against a mock is replaced.
---
